With both `--lemma-bindings` and `--member-invariants`, the member-invariant
extension check now also covers the proofs that justify a lemma binding in an
invariant's cone: the bound lemma's body, the proof hints of the functions in
the cone, and the lemmas they call. It rejects an out-parameter of the bound
lemma whose type depends on the invariant's type, and, in those proofs, raw
tests and conversions, choices of a value of that type, and reads of a field or
array element of that type from the heap. Without these checks, a result of
such a type, a raw test, a heap read or a `:|` choice in such a proof can prove
`false`.
